A solver option that selects Z3's int-blasting bit-vector solver, `smt.bv.solver=2`, is now an error. With Z3 5.1.0 that solver reports satisfiable queries of the shape Dafny emits for bit-vector subtraction as unsatisfiable, so `dafny verify` accepted `assert false` after `var z := x - y` on `bv8` to `bv64` values. The option is rejected before verification in every spelling Z3 accepts, whether it comes from `--solver-option`, `--boogie /proverOpt:`, the legacy `/proverOpt:` or a project file. The hidden `--legacy-allow-unsound-bv-solver` accepts it, with a warning that the results are untrusted, for migration and comparison only (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/618).
